  "real_regression_fixed": {
    "symptom": "After first successful group stop/continue, later thread-directed TSTP remained pending forever on a parked member. Tracing could hide the race.",
    "cause": "A STOP wake remained fired when the task parked; subsequent CONT and catchable-stop wakes were coalesced into the old notification.",
    "fix": "Rearm the original task signal under the run-queue mutex before final level-state checks at parking/custody boundaries. No new wake transport or polling thread.",
    "regression": "Four consecutive stop/wait/continue/wait cycles with one and four executor slots; zero owner requests."
  },
